module dev.slatelang.slate

import sysl.buf.{Buf, buf}

// What a string literal is at run time: ONE cell per literal, made the first time the literal runs
// and handed out every time after.
//
// **`PushStr` USED TO MAKE A FRESH `StrObj` ON EVERY EXECUTION**, so `{ proto: Counter, n: n }` in a
// constructor built two string cells per object for its two keys, and `line.split(",")` one per line
// for the comma -- text that cannot change, allocated, charged, traced and swept again on every turn.
// On `bench/calls.sl` that was two of the three allocations per construction.
//
// **Sharing one cell is sound because a string cell cannot be changed by anything a program does.**
// Its text is fixed when it is made (`str_room.sysl` appends past the END of a room and never writes
// a byte any string can see), a program cannot tell two cells of equal text apart -- equality is by
// text, and a weak map refuses a string key for exactly that reason (`weak.sysl`) -- and the two
// fields that do change, the character cursor, are a cache of where the last index landed, right for
// any reader of the same text.
//
// **The table is the machine's, not the unit's**, because the cells are heap objects and the unit is
// not traced: `Vm.literals` is a root walked beside `Vm.defs`, and `reset_vm` empties it with the
// rest of what a run left behind -- which is also what keeps an index from outliving the unit whose
// numbering it is in. An actor's machine has a unit and a table of its own, so no cell crosses a heap.

// The cell literal `k` of `u` is. `u` is the machine's own `current_unit`, as it is for every chunk
// the machine runs.
literal_on(here: *Vm, u: *Unit, k: usize) -> Value
    if k < here.literals.len()
        here.literals.at(k) match
            Undefined -> ()
            v -> return v

    literal_made(here, u, k)
end literal_on

// The first execution of a literal: make its cell and keep it.
//
// **Nothing between making the cell and keeping it can collect**: the table grows outside the
// collected heap, and the places it grows by hold `Undefined`, which `mark_value` passes over.
private literal_made(here: *Vm, u: *Unit, k: usize) -> Value
    val made = str_counted(u.strings.at(k), u.string_chars.at(k))

    while here.literals.len() <= k
        here.literals.push(Undefined)

    here.literals.set(k, made)
    made
end literal_made
